## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* a path beyond the one, or any product, support, tooling, workflow, package or lock file in the PR; a removed line of main outside the claimed regions that is not a comment you judge; the checker, `AUDIT_STEPS` values, `put`, row P, an R or T row loosened or changed; an existing name lost or a base title changed; an added name other than the named row; a skip, `.only`, environment gate, sleep or provider branch; **a named target mutant SURVIVING at the head** (N1-N6, job-if, job-needs, job-coe, prod-env, dev-uses, dev-dupkey, dev-removed: P, the R/T rows and the derived rows must go red) **or an equivalent (eq-comment-in, eq-comment-above, eq-quote, eq-trailing, eq-blank) turning ANY row of the head file red**; **a mutant or plant that went from red at the base to green at the head and is neither a two-place legitimate edit nor an equivalent (a lost kill)**; a derived row green for the wrong reason or never red under any mutant, plant or disk run and not a declared control; **the regression row not red under CM-s or under the base renderer**; a new write, removal, spawn, request, listener, port literal or check-then-use pair; a raw non-ASCII byte in an added line; a ticket key, card id or person name in an added line or the commit message; a secret; the head moved; a red check-run; **a CodeQL alert open on the head or the merge ref (either threshold), a missing analysis at the verdict, or a dismissed alert the gate did not make but the count shows**; a textual conflict in Check 8; **the head test going red against main's real `ci.yml`**. *Major (state SAME or DIFFERENT class as this lane's class "the audit-dev rows derive from `AUDIT_STEPS`"):* **SAME class: any round-trip plant (name, run, key in any position, multiline, X2, special, nested, coe-false, collide, two, all-three, block-nested, first-oneline, first-empty) that leaves ANY of the 41 rows red after the two-place edit; any equivalent edit that reddens a row; the renderer yielding a document the parser or the checker refuses for a table shape the header comment calls legitimate (X-keep judged legitimate); `put` throwing for a table entry the file's own comment calls legitimate.** **DIFFERENT class: a drift plant (D1-D4) or L2 leaving the 25 not red (the pin can drift); a builder claim contradicted by measurement (the 25-red fan-out, the 28 of CM-h/CM-i, the 2938 count, names lost 0 / added 1, the 50 repeats if you can show one red); a repeat red; `yaml`'s `stringify` resolving under one pool only; the web unit job's counts not +1 over the push run on `754bf1e7`.** *Minor/Note:* the weakening trade of 4e (a Note carrying the stamp's ruling); GB1-GB4 surviving; the 25-red fan-out for one drift (rows share one premise); CM-k/l/m unkilled guard lines; the unreachable `throw` in `put` (CM-r 0); a third audit step turning the E rows red; `lineWidth: 0` not load-bearing; X-keep if judged not legitimate; unsigned commit; the trailer naming a model other than the kit's; the PR title/body carrying a ticket key and a builder id; the builder's 50-run repeats cut to your 10; a count that differs from the builder's with no verdict consequence.
